1:/* server_ready.c: the readiness snapshot sampler behind GET /v1/ready.
2: *
3: * The route (server_http.c) must not perform dependency I/O — a wedged
4: * dependency would otherwise stall the listener — so this unit samples each
5: * dependency on a background interval and publishes an immutable snapshot the
6: * route can read in O(1). This is also why the sampler lives here rather than
7: * in server_http.c: it pulls the kb_client/db1 dependency closure that
8: * server_http.c and its unit test deliberately stay free of.
9: *
10: * Dependencies sampled:
11: *   db1  — db1_is_initialized(). Deliberately a no-I/O check, not the
12: *          store/load/remove round-trip `aimee doctor` uses: doctor runs once
13: *          on demand, this runs on a timer, and a periodic write probe would
14: *          make the readiness endpoint its own source of load.
15: *   kb   — kb_client_health(). One HTTP call to aimee-kb, off the request path.
16: *
17: * The retrieval contract additionally requires the KB schema/vector collection
18: * and embedder advertised by KB health, plus a non-open E5a transport breaker.
19: * This is readiness, not liveness: a recoverable dependency outage drains work
20: * without asking the supervisor to restart a healthy server process.
21: *
22: * Fail-closed rules:
23: *   - before the first sample completes, every dependency is `unknown` and the
24: *     server is NOT ready (an unsampled server must never read as ready);
25: *   - a snapshot older than the staleness bound degrades back to `unknown`, so
26: *     a wedged sampler cannot leave a stale "ready" standing forever;
27: *   - the roll-up is ready only when every dependency sampled `ok`.
28: *
29: * Tuning (env, so an operator can adjust without a rebuild; conservative
30: * defaults chosen so the probe never becomes load):
31: *   AIMEE_READY_INTERVAL_SECS  sampling period  (default 15, range 1..3600)
32: *   AIMEE_READY_STALE_SECS     staleness bound  (default 60, range interval..86400)
33: */
34:#include "server_http.h"
35:#include "kb_client.h"
36:#include "db1.h"
37:#include "log.h"
38:#include <pthread.h>
39:#include <stdio.h>
40:#include <errno.h>
41:#include <stdlib.h>
42:#include <string.h>
43:#include <time.h>
44:#include <unistd.h>
